From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Feb 2023 14:25:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: add STA-assisted DFS state update

An extender runs a STA and an AP on the same DFS channel. The root AP
of the STA already did the CAC and runs radar detection there.
Without help, the extender AP starts its own CAC after each switch
to a DFS channel.

The STA marks the channels of its BSS and of a CSA target available;
the target keeps that state until the switch completes. When the STA
leaves, an available 20 MHz channel becomes usable again, unless the
CSA target, an AP or the background chain covers it. The CSA target
check comes from mtk-openwrt-feeds 2df62b873dd2,
0023-mtk-mac80211-add-sta-assisted-DFS-state-update-mecha.patch
("mtk: mac80211: add sta-assisted DFS state update mechanism"). Each
BSS channel that changes gets its own event, because hostapd applies
an event to every channel of its chandef. An AP on the band and radio
of the channel gets each event, because only the hostapd instance of
that interface handles it. A local radar event, not a background one
in atomic context, keeps channels that the STA covers available,
because the root AP saw no radar.

Signed-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
